    affiliation: The University of Melbourne
repository-code: "https://github.com/evenodderguy/maver"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  MAVER diagnoses and repairs live Kubernetes microservice incidents with a pipeline of
  typed roles driven by a privately served open-weight language model. The default
  workflow separates diagnosis, planning and execution. A stage-aware approval gate
  restricts classified Kubernetes API mutations to execution, which applies its plan
  under a check-and-set discipline. Pod execution requires human approval by default.
  Optional mechanisms add an independent verification role that can hand work back and
  a gated second diagnostic opinion informed by an experience store of past incidents.
keywords:
  - incident response
  - site reliability engineering
  - kubernetes
  - large language model agents
  - retrieval-augmented generation
